% M7-T33 / D-0156: an all_different STAGE-1 conflict under a decision now LEARNS.
%
% Deciding k <= 2 makes the three int_le push x1, x2, x3 <= 2 before the all_different they
% wake runs (FIFO: each watches k and one x), so the Hall interval 1..2 holds three
% variables. Until M7-T33 that pigeonhole was a push that must fail, paired with
% Reason.none, so the branch closed on the full decision nogood and nothing was learned.
% Now it is reported with its facts -- both bounds of the surplus variable and of the Hall
% set, x1..x3 <= 2 -- and its derivation is written ahead of `rup ~facts >= 1`
% (Store.deriving_ahead, D-0096), so 1UIP learning resolves from it (learned 2: k >= 2 and
% k >= 3).
%
% SAT, so the database is not contradictory and every rup on the page is really checked
% (D-0053, D-0066/D-0073). test_prop.ml's M7-T33 lanes pin the k <= 2 conflict line and
% refuse it standalone, without its pol, and with its last fact dropped.
var 1..4: k :: output_var;
var 1..4: x1 :: output_var;
var 1..4: x2 :: output_var;
var 1..4: x3 :: output_var;
constraint int_le(x1,k);
constraint int_le(x2,k);
constraint int_le(x3,k);
constraint all_different_int([x1,x2,x3]);
solve :: int_search([k,x1,x2,x3], input_order, indomain_min, complete) satisfy;
